codeExercise.solutionNote:
Used in a loader:

```js
async function attachHosts(db, episodes) {
  const ids = planHostFetch(episodes);
  if (ids.length === 0) return [];
  const hosts = await db.hostsByIds(ids);          // exactly one query
  const byId = new Map(hosts.map(h => [h.id, h.name]));
  return episodes.map(e => ({ ...e, hostName: byId.get(e.hostId) ?? null }));
}
```

Note `?? null` rather than leaving it `undefined` — Section 2's predict-run showed that an `undefined` value deletes the key from the serialized response entirely.

